9d7","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/Gusted","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2021-04-12T21:28:08+02:00","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"Error 451","pronouns":"","website":"https://gusted.xyz","description":"I’m aware (and the NSA is), that I’m pretty 🌈.\r\n\r\nForgejo contributor  \r\nCodeberg executive board member 2025-2026  \r\nCodeberg presidium member 2025-2027  \r\n\r\nFor more interesting repositories: https://git.gusted.xyz/Gusted","visibility":"public","followers_count":163,"following_count":30,"starred_repos_count":104,"username":"Gusted"},"body":"\u003e The complexity of the function being modified is very high. It would help review and make sure that allowing this to go through does not have unintended side effects if either you could confirm there is test coverage for all of it or by explaining how you evaluated the impact.\r\n\r\nSurprisingly there were already test coverage for the other function that are involved to handle commit IDs, it just so happens that that specific web route didn't knew it could allow it. The UI was already adopted for it and tags on commits are already stored via the release table, so the database code for releases is also already compatible with it. It's actually quite mindbogglingly how this wasn't fixed earlier. ","created_at":"2023-08-05T21:30:54+02:00","updated_at":"2023-08-05T21:30:54+02:00","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":null,"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"none","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":null,"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":1020070,"type":"review","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/1200#issuecomment-1020070","pull_request_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/1200","issue_url":"","us